      "title": "The finite image and separated twisted norms",
      "anchor": "inputs-detecting-classes",
      "statement": "For an enlarged totally complex field L′ and a cyclic layer F with μ_q, choose one element of F× with a twisted principal divisor for each element of a finite powered-norm image. Distinct representatives have distinct ℓ^b-powered twisted norms modulo qth powers. The bound on such sets bounds the whole image.",
      "hypotheses": "q=ℓ^ν, ν≥c≥1 (c≥2 when ℓ=2); γ generates Gal(F/L′), sends ζ to ζ^(1+ℓ^c), and has order ℓ^(ν−c). e≥1, m=2e+1<min(ℓ^c,r₂(L′)), a=(1+ℓ^c)^e, b=2e+m(c+m). Distinguish the finite set S from the group of equivariant class characters. The target for the finite image f also kills roots of unity.",
      "definitions": [
        "twisted norm",
        "twisted principal divisor",
        "separated set",
        "finite image",
        "power and torsion quotient"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-detecting-norm"
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
