    {
      "id": "DET-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A weighted prism detects the residue index",
      "anchor": "inputs-detecting-prism",
      "statement": "For a representing α there is an integral-matrix-group cycle yα with Z/q coefficients whose evaluation at an allowed residue field is D_e times the index of N_a(α). Equal ℓ^(2e)-scaled evaluations imply the powered norm ratio is locally a qth power.",
      "hypotheses": "Same cyclic layer and separation data. Finite residue field away from ℓ and common denominators, with surjective reduction of O_L′. q divides the residue unit group order. Primitive index functional with qth powers as kernel, evaluation family additive and killing boundaries. Existence of cycle relations and prescribed determinants is supplied.",
      "definitions": [
        "weighted prism",
        "cyclic index",
        "primitive residue root",
        "polynomial value D_e",
        "ℓ-adic divisibility"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-detecting-evaluation"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "DET-01",
        "CYC-02",
        "CYC-04",
        "DIP-03",
        "GLU-03"
      ],
      "correspondence": "The difference of two fillings and the weighted prisms has zero boundary. Its normalization by a unit realizes an integral group cycle. Evaluation removes indices of determinant-one terms and keeps the distinguished block. D_e divides ℓ^(m(c+m)) in Z/q by bounding ordℓ of κ^d−1 for 0<d<m. Multiplication by that complementary factor transfers congruence of evaluations to congruence of powered norm indices. In F19×, index modulo 9 takes the same value on 2^8 and 2^17.",
