  "outstanding": [
    "CYC-01–04 construct the cyclic relation and residue determinant test. DIP-01–03 give interpolation and the weighted-norm formula. GLU-01–03 and SDN-01–02 supply integral gluing, free stabilization, a common denominator and the split residue comparison.",
    "Chebotarev density at rational degree-one primes is used as a specifically named theorem. The local-to-global power detection argument from that theorem is reconstructed.",
    "STB-01–02 derive the filtered rank bound. SEL-01–02 account for the complementary norm kernel and unit factor in the independent character count."
  ],
  "review_scope": "Followed the SClass, SDetect, SFew, SUpper and SCount witnesses to the degree-two application; translated source e_inner to the positive twist e_inner+1 used in NumThree."
